>>
Rule 1 (tensor dtype must be float or complex as required by SVD)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 2 (avoid device errors by disallowing float16 inputs)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 6
>>
Rule 3 (input must represent matrices or a stack of matrices: rank ≥ 2)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 4 (all dimensions, including the last two matrix dimensions, must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 5 (only compute full-sized factors when singular vectors are requested)
{v_2 : bool, v_3 : bool} |= if v_2 then v_3
>>
Rule 6 (operation name limited to known strings)
{v_4 : str} |= v_4 = "none" ∨ v_4 = "linear" ∨ v_4 = "sum" ∨ v_4 = "max" ∨ v_4 = "min"
